From: Qianhui Xu <xiaqinghuan@mail.ustc.edu.cn>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 20:28:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali: describe the TNOC AMBA
 periphid

The aggregator TNOC at 111b8000 is an AMBA device, but its node carries
no "arm,primecell-periphid", so the AMBA core falls back to whatever
the integration leaves in the peripheral ID register.  As observed on
SM8750, whose TNOC is wired up the same way, that reads back as
0x00000000 and coresight-tnoc (which matches 0x000f0c00/0x001f0c00 with
mask 0x00ffff00) then never probes, leaving the node as
"deferred probe pending: (reason unknown)".

Describe the ID the driver expects, as is already done for the SM8750
TNOC and for the SM8250 funnels.

*** AI-assistance disclosure ***
This patch was prepared with the help of an LLM coding assistant.  The
author reviewed every line and ran dtbs_check and checkpatch.

Signed-off-by: Qianhui Xu <xiaqinghuan@mail.ustc.edu.cn>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
index e48a179d0722..f9ae46b90d16 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
@@ -5416,6 +5416,7 @@ tpdm_pcie_rscc_out: endpoint {
 		tn@111b8000 {
 			compatible = "qcom,coresight-tnoc", "arm,primecell";
 			reg = <0x0 0x111b8000 0x0 0x4200>;
+			arm,primecell-periphid = <0x000f0c00>;
 
 			clocks = <&aoss_qmp>;
 			clock-names = "apb_pclk";
